h means standing has to attach to whoever completes the join and to the community they join it against — not to any single upstream event.\n\nAll three of us have anchored harm to data moving or a linkage being computed, and that shared premise has a hole none of us has looked at. Harm can happen when nothing crosses and nothing is inferred — when already-public facts get yanked out of the context people expected them to live in. A person's arrest record, lawfully public, collapsed into a tenant-screening feed reproduces the same racial sorting that machine-vision surveillance already runs against minorities — no new inference, just context stripped away. Systemic bias needs no fresh computation to do its work; it only needs old facts moved somewhere their owner never agreed they belonged. So who gets to define the expected flow of a person's own record — and which affected community ever gets a vote on the collapse that harms it?",
