  "statement": "The core privacy blind spot is that policymakers built recourse around the moment of denial, and the person who is scored, priced, and watched but never formally rejected walks out of the frame entirely. The Skeptic is right on the narrow point I have to concede first: membership inference — the statistical test that shows a person's data sits inside a training corpus — detects a population pattern. It does not hand any individual a letter. A regulator who runs that test gets a prosecutable pattern, not a named woman to notify. Inspectability is not accountability, and I said so earlier; a detection method that flags the pattern is not the same instrument as a notice that reaches the subject. So the honest answer is that my membership-inference test, by itself, never reaches her.\n\nThe notify-duty does reach her — but only in one of two classes, and the split is the whole argument. Split the market. In the priced-sale class, an auxiliary-data broker already holds the named linkage when it prices and sells it; the identifier is in the broker's hands at the moment of the transaction. Notifying that woman requires no fresh re-identification, because the broker already knows who she is when it sells the record. The enrollment-ignorance trap — the objection that you cannot notify her without first re-identifying her — dissolves here, because the re-identification already happened inside the broker's own ledger before any agent ran. In the fused-weights class, identity sits absorbed into trained model weights with no broker query and no discrete sale to trigger on; there, the duty fires blank. For the record: the notify-duty reaches the never-denied woman in the priced-sale class and inherits the ignorance failure in the fused-weights class.\n\nThe Skeptic located the true chokepoint correctly, and I am moving to it. The injury is manufactured upstream in the broker market where linkage is priced before any agent executes — regulating the last-mile agent's transfer does nothing about that infrastructure. So the eligibility bar and the notify-duty belong at a registrable broker class, on the Vermont data-broker registry model that has required brokers to register since 2019, not at the agent. That relocation is the exact decoupling the Skeptic flagged in his own position: the duty fires on the recorded linkage-sale, not on a denial event, not on her enrollment. An external oversight body — a registrable-broker regime with a named registrant, not a subject-initiated request — is the institutional form that survives the subsidiary shuffle, because the obligation attaches to whoever prices the linkage.\n\nHere is the one condition that closes the gap. The notify-duty must attach to a registrable broker holding the linkage independent of any request from the subject, backed by strict liability for operating without provenance — so the trigger fires on the recorded sale of the named linkage. No act by the woman is required. No new re-identification is required. The broker already holds her identity when it prices the record; the strict-liability anchor makes the sale itself the reportable event. That is what converts population-level detection into a per-subject notice, and it is the single feature both sides agreed neither of us had.\n\nThe broker-market audit resolves the residual. If a buyer fuses independently-clean corpora inside trained weights — where the linkage never crosses a sale a regulator can see — the linkage-sale trigger weakens and the agent's own transfer becomes the regulable event instead. If recombination-at-sale dominates the market, the broker chokepoint and the notify-duty hold. The 2025 Foundation Model Transparency Index scored the ecosystem at 40.69 out of 100, so no one should assume the fusion path is already visible — the audit is what makes the choice between the two triggers on evidence, not on a vendor's word. Whichever way that audit falls, the freeze on the irreversible subset — mass re-identification, bulk exfiltration — stays. You can debate where the notice fires. You cannot undo a population that has been permanently re-identified.",
