  "statement": "I concede the symmetry: if linkage keys move through bundled, barter, or intra-affiliate transfers, standing-at-the-broker inherits the same reachability failure I pinned on the opt-in registry, and the woman who never learns a broker holds her file never learns to contest it. I still hold that notice-and-standing is owed wherever the harm actually completes and cannot be prevented, because a barred capability is not the same thing as a person who gets to know and get paid. I would abandon the licensed-broker class the moment someone shows me the key-holders sit inside conglomerates, across borders, or in entities that never register — because then the class is undefinable and the anchor has to move to the one act that cannot relocate.\n\nHere is my verdict on the original question. The core blind spot policymakers should anticipate is that the privacy harm from AI agents forms at the join, not the sale, and no gate anyone in this room has proposed watches the join. The broker layer is where racial sorting gets priced and sold, and Vermont proved a class is partly nameable — 121 brokers registered under its 2018 law. But a concentrated market writes its own definitions. When a handful of firms control the aggregation layer, they capture the rule that says who must register, and the conglomerate subsidiary that never files becomes the escape hatch. That is why the duty has to attach to a fixed in-jurisdiction act — deployment, market entry — that a corporate parent cannot move offshore to dodge.\n\nThe unresolved crux is not our theories. It is a number nobody in this room has produced: the actual transaction structure of the broker market. If linkage keys mostly change hands through priced sales, a sale-trigger reaches them. If they move through intra-affiliate barter, every sale-anchored control fires blank. Provenance metadata verifies where a corpus came from, but it cannot foresee which clean file fuses with a second clean file to re-identify a person downstream. A stamp confirms origin. It says nothing about the linkage that materializes three transactions later. Demand the transaction number before anyone declares a mechanism the winner.\n\nWhere the Safetyist narrowed the eligibility bar to the non-consented irreversible re-identification class, that prevents completion, and I will not put a notify duty on a harm that never happens. That mechanism is superior for that scope precisely because there is no injury to notice. Hold the line where completion is not preventable. The arrest-record case is the wound none of the three gates reaches: a lawfully-public record pulled into a tenant-screening feed, no data crossing, nothing computed, reproducing the racial sorting that the NEJM race-adjusted algorithm work documents — where a formula assigned black patients lower risk scores and delayed their referral for specialist care. Post-hoc audit detects that sorting pattern. It never tells the person their arrest record got recontextualized, and it never gives them standing to fight it. So the question I leave with all three: which mechanism tells that person, and lets them contest it, when no data moved and nothing was computed?",
