s transfer does nothing about that infrastructure. So the eligibility bar and the notify-duty belong at a registrable broker class, on the Vermont data-broker registry model that has required brokers to register since 2019, not at the agent. That relocation is the exact decoupling the Skeptic flagged in his own position: the duty fires on the recorded linkage-sale, not on a denial event, not on her enrollment. An external oversight body — a registrable-broker regime with a named registrant, not a subject-initiated request — is the institutional form that survives the subsidiary shuffle, because the obligation attaches to whoever prices the linkage.\n\nHere is the one condition that closes the gap. The notify-duty must attach to a registrable broker holding the linkage independent of any request from the subject, backed by strict liability for operating without provenance — so the trigger fires on the recorded sale of the named linkage. No act by the woman is required. No new re-identification is required. The broker already holds her identity when it prices the record; the strict-liability anchor makes the sale itself the reportable event. That is what converts population-level detection into a per-subject notice, and it is the single feature both sides agreed neither of us had.\n\nThe broker-market audit resolves the residual. If a buyer fuses independently-clean corpora inside trained weights — where the linkage never crosses a sale a regulator can see — the linkage-sale trigger weakens and the agent's own transfer becomes the regulable event instead. If recombination-at-sale dominates the market, the broker chokepoint and the notify-duty hold. The 2025 Foundation Model Transparency Index scored the ecosystem at 40.69 out of 100, so no one should assume the fusion path is already visible — the audit is what makes the choice between the two triggers on evidence, not on a vendor's word. Whichever way that audit falls, the freeze on the irreversible subset — mass re-identification, bulk exfiltration — stays. You can debate where the notice fires. You cannot undo a population that has been permanently re-identified.",
